// A path element is a name, and a name can end a statement, so the newline
// after one ends the declaration. `import` asked that and `use` did not, so a
// re-export reached down a line and exported whatever it found there: this
// compiled clean and ran, re-exporting `mm.thing` from a line the author had
// separated.
//
// The formatter then rewrote the two lines into one, which is a tool that
// writes in place deleting a line break its own purpose says it must keep. The
// hatch could not see it either -- what it compares is the already-joined tree
// against itself.
//
// The sibling cases pin the terminator half for both forms. This is the half
// that was left: which run of tokens the path is.
import mm
pub use mm
.thing

fn main() -> UInt8 {
    thing()
}
